* text=auto

*.js text
*.html text
*.less text
*.json text
*.css text
*.xml text
# TASK 4.7. Vendored third-party libraries are byte-exact copies of upstream
# releases, and their md5s are the acceptance criterion for the shipped tree
# (PHASE1-TREE.md). The `*.js text` rule above would normalise them: form2js and
# js2form are CRLF upstream, so git would store LF-only blobs and a fresh clone
# would build a tree whose form2js is 8c993db9 rather than the pinned 897ec696.
# That silently undoes the reason those two are vendored at all -- see
# src/main/js/libs/README.md and NOTES-libs-retire.md sections 7 and 16.
# `-text` disables eol conversion but keeps them diffable.
src/main/js/libs/** -text
src/main/resources/css/bootstrap-datetimepicker-4.14.30-min.css -text

# Not vendored: this project's own source and our own register. Normal rules.
src/main/js/libs/README.md text
src/main/js/libs/popover-clickaway.js text
